  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (RNA-only, multi-profile, PCA_n2000, avgpool) is the current best at 0.591 acc, showing a large ~10.6% gain over single-profile PCA (config_001, 0.485). This strongly suggests multi-profile aggregation is a key design lever. Uncertainty: we do not yet know whether a more expressive aggregation (transformer) can further improve over simple avgpool in the multi-profile setting, or whether avgpool already captures most of the benefit. This experiment (config_003) changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding model setting, profile setting, and encoder fixed to the best-known combination, giving a clean single-variable comparison. It is the best use of the next budget slot because it directly extends the strongest evidence, isolates the aggregation effect, and the result will inform all subsequent multi-profile and multimodal experiments (configs 020, 021, 026, 027, etc.) where aggregation choice is a critical design decision."
}

